`LogNorm` is defined in `colors.py` via `make_norm_from_scale(functools.partial(scale.LogScale, nonpositive="mask"))`. The generated norm stores a `LogScale` instance and its transform, and in `__call__` it explicitly evaluates `self._trf.transform(value)` as well as transforming `vmin` and `vmax`. In `scale.py`, `LogScale.get_transform()` returns a `LogTransform`, and the forward `LogTransform.transform_non_affine` at the referenced site is the method that applies the logarithm to input values. Since the test calls `axes[1].imshow(z, norm=matplotlib.colors.LogNorm())` on strictly positive data, that forward log-transform site is reached during the test.

